3:T479,This hidden gem is a whole new pottery experience. Nestled in a lush, leafy garden in Tiong Bahru, you'll spend a blissful few hours getting your hands delightfully muddy under the expert eye of a true creative designer. Forget run-of-the-mill bowls and mugs – think quirky sloth cups, or plates adorned with your gorgeous fur babies. This is hand-building pottery with an extra dose of personality!



What to expect

Leave everyday stress at the garden gate – this is your creative oasis.
Learn the ancient art of hand-building pottery – no intimidating wheels here!
Let your imagination run wild – your host will guide you to bring those unique piece ideas to life.
Celebrate a special occasion? You can customize your ceramic creation for birthdays, proposals...the sky's the limit!
Kiddos in tow? They'll love this pottery adventure where they create and paint their piece in one fun session.


Important tips

This cozy experience needs at least 2 people to run. Perfect for a creative date or gathering a small group of friends!
Your one-of-a-kind masterpieces will need 3-4 weeks for glazing and firing before you take them home.4:T4d7,What you will learn Choose the Best Salad greens for Singapore’s climate that are delicious and healthy  (e.g. right varieties of lettuce, kale…and many others) Using Sunlight to keep your cost low in hydroponics No soil, no mess – just clean, fast, space-saving growing Understand Safety in Hydroponics – we teach you how to identify safe materials to use in hydropoics Plant, Grow, and Harvest with confidence—learn when to sow, how to water, and when to harvest for maximum flavor and nutrition. Grow in Small Spaces using our techniques, ideal for balconies, HDB flats, condominium .  Techniques also applies to landed property What's Included 25 Comprehensive Video Lessons covering every stage of your hydroponics salad greens journey. Total Duration is 2 Hours.  Access anytime , anywhere for the entire 1 year Downloadable Slides, Guides & Checklists so you can follow along easily even at the end of the course. Early Bird BONUS #1  GrowThrive Hydroponics Kit (include all you need to start hydroponics at home) Worth SG$45 (only during promo period) Early Bird BONUS #2 FREE One year one-to-one support from Expert Training Team (You can ask them questions and they support you to grow salad greens using hydroponics!) 0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"listings":[{"id":"8","slug":"amazing-race-singapore","title":"Amazing Race SG","provider":"Rally Co.","category":"Adventure","location":"City-wide","duration":"3.5h","price":40,"pax":"15–60","featured":true,"tags":["team-bonding","active"],"description":"A city-wide scavenger hunt across Singapore's neighbourhoods. Clues, checkpoints, and a fair amount of arguing about which MRT line to take. Good luck!","image":"/images/1779196599007-x0wm9o9ugrq.jpg","images":[],"host":{"name":"The Rally Co. Team","bio":"Rally Co. has been running city-wide adventure experiences across Singapore since 2015. Their facilitators are ex-event producers and avid urban explorers who know every shortcut, hawker stall, and hidden corner of the island."},"whatToExpect":"Your team will be split into groups of 5–8 and handed a sealed envelope at the starting point. Inside: your first clue.\n\nOver 3.5 hours you'll navigate across 6–8 checkpoints spread across Singapore's neighbourhoods — on foot, MRT, and the occasional taxi scramble. Each checkpoint has a challenge: a trivia question, a physical task, or a local vendor you need to track down.\n\nThe winning team gets bragging rights and a group photo at the finish line. Every team gets a debrief with the funniest moments from the day."},{"id":"3","featured":false,"slug":"kintsugi","title":"Kintsugi Art Studio","provider":"Kintsugi Art Studio","image":"/images/896e51_7583ce0d6b334e078b19cbdd10ddadb4~mv2.avif","description":"Kintsugi is Japan's ancient art of celebrating broken pottery. It is rooted in an eastern philosophy of finding beauty in imperfections. Many believe it can help us to accept our flaws and foster a sense of peace and fulfillment.\n\nhttps://www.kintsugiartstudio.com/","category":"Pottery","location":"Joo Chiat","duration":"3h","price":95,"pax":"1–12","tags":["emotional","educational","solo"],"images":[],"host":{"name":"The Kintsugi Team","bio":"The Kintsugi Art Studio team are passionate practitioners of the Japanese art form, trained in both the traditional urushi lacquer technique and modern adaptations. They believe the practice of repair is as meaningful as the object itself."},"whatToExpect":"You'll begin by selecting a piece of broken pottery — or bringing your own — and understanding the philosophy behind kintsugi: that breakage and repair are part of an object's history, not something to hide.\n\nUsing a food-safe, non-toxic lacquer mixed with gold powder, you'll carefully fill each crack with deliberate brushwork. The process is meditative and unhurried.\n\nYour piece will need 24–48 hours to cure fully. The studio will wrap it carefully for transport. You'll leave with both the repaired piece and a deeper appreciation for imperfection."},{"id":"4","slug":"candle-workshop-bugis","title":"One-of-a-kind pottery in Tiong Bahru | Lush Garden, Kid-friendly (4+)","provider":"Wax & Wick","category":"Craft","location":"Bugis","duration":"2h","price":55,"pax":"1–15","featured":false,"tags":["burned-out","introvert","creative"],"description":"$3","image":"/images/1779195308150-m00l6elnni.webp","images":["/images/1779195322907-jd95b3w6kg8.webp","/images/1779195327758-571gn2sgsgu.webp","/images/1779195332348-wkm9b34zsup.webp"],"host":{"name":"Emily Lim","bio":"Emily's backyard pottery studio is a hidden gem! A former creative designer, she's got a knack for turning your wildest ideas into beautiful ceramic pieces. Emily's warm, patient style and years of experience make her the perfect guide on your pottery journey."},"whatToExpect":"You'll arrive to a studio that smells unreasonably good. After a short intro on wax types and fragrance blending, you'll choose your scent combination from over 30 options and pick your vessel — from classic tins to ceramic pots.\n\nThe pouring process takes about 45 minutes. While your candle sets, Sarah walks you through care tips: why cotton wicks matter, how to get a clean burn, and how to re-use the vessel once the wax is gone.\n\nYou'll leave with one completed candle (plus any extras you make if time allows). No experience needed — if you can pour a cup of coffee, you can make a candle."},{"id":"6","slug":"escape-room-clarke-quay","title":"Singapore Wake Park","provider":"Singapore Wake Park","category":"Adventure","location":"East Coast Park","duration":"2h","price":45,"pax":"6–30","featured":true,"tags":["team-bonding","active"],"description":"The Park features two straight-line systems. System A (60 meters) is designed for complete beginners, offering wakeboarding lessons led by our experienced instructors.\n\nThe system runs one rider at a time, providing a safe, focused learning environment with full instructor attention. Its gradual cable speed makes learning the basics easier, making it ideal for young children.\n\nThe Park runs 9 lessons daily, each lasting 1 hour, with a maximum of 4 riders per lesson.\n\nRate:\n$55 per rider/hour or 1 hour off Share-The-Fun Pass\nIncludes: Helmet, Vest & House Wakeboard (Non-Obstacle)\nObstacle Wakeboard Rental: $20/Session\n\n- Rate is inclusive of GST & applicable daily\n- Recommended age for a participating child is 6 years old & above\n- All riders are required to know basic swimming","image":"/images/1779195581152-78v53o6w5im.webp","images":["/images/1779195590247-otdc55t093l.jpg","/images/1779195604160-6hh5m5ai2qg.jpg"],"host":{"name":"Wakeboard Singapore","bio":"The Locked SG team are puzzle designers, ex-corporate trainers, and enthusiastic chaos-causers. They've run over 500 team sessions and know exactly which moments reveal who your team really is under pressure."},"whatToExpect":"Your group will be briefed on the scenario — typically a 60-minute escape challenge designed for 6–12 people simultaneously. Unlike solo escape rooms, this one is built for collaboration: clues are distributed across the team from the start.\n\nAfter the room, a trained facilitator runs a 30-minute structured debrief. It's not a post-mortem — it's a genuine conversation about communication styles, decision-making under pressure, and what your team learned about itself.\n\nNo escape room experience needed. First-timers often have the most interesting debrief moments."},{"id":"5","slug":"hawker-cook-off-various","title":"One Day Scuba Singapore","provider":"The Dive company","category":"Sports","location":"Regional (island-wide)","duration":"3h","price":55,"pax":"10–40","featured":true,"tags":["active","introvert"],"description":"🇸🇬 Singapore-Based Open Water Course‍  ‍\n\nTrain and certify entirely in Singapore - perfect for tight schedules or local convenience.","image":"/images/1779196126392-zy0n6g92z89.jpg","images":["/images/1779196131082-f6zxb6dgyhb.jpg","/images/1779196136217-0uhla6qarur.jpg","/images/1779196146786-8824f55o39o.jpg"],"host":{"name":"Scuba Singapore","bio":"Team Kopi are Singapore-born food educators who've spent years documenting hawker recipes before they disappear. They run the cook-off as a love letter to hawker culture — competitive, loud, and delicious."},"whatToExpect":"Trying scuba for the first time can feel intimidating — but you're not alone. We’ve helped thousands of first-time divers become confident and certified.\n\nHere’s why beginners choose us:\n\n✅ Friendly, certified instructors who know how to coach first-timers  \n\n✅ Step-by-step training, starting in a shallow pool  \n\n✅ All dive equipment provided — just bring swimwear and curiosity  \n\n✅ Choose between local or tropical open water locations\n\nWe’ll support you every step of the way, from your first breath underwater to your final qualifying dive."},{"id":"7","slug":"improv-for-workplaces-cbd","title":"Improv for Workplaces","provider":"Yes And SG","category":"Wellness","location":"CBD","duration":"3h","price":65,"pax":"10–30","featured":false,"tags":["team-bonding","educational"],"description":"No scripts, no presentations — just your team learning to listen, adapt, and say yes to each other. Improv exercises that translate directly into better collaboration.","image":"/images/1779196528728-u3m16t1k8oe.webp","images":[],"host":{"name":"The Yes And SG Collective","bio":"Yes And SG is Singapore's longest-running workplace improv company, founded by actors, coaches, and one former management consultant who got tired of PowerPoint. Their facilitators have worked with teams from MNCs to scrappy startups."},"whatToExpect":"The session opens with low-stakes warm-up games — think word-association and mirroring exercises — designed to get people out of their heads and into the room.\n\nFrom there, the facilitators introduce the core improv principle: 'Yes, and.' Every scene builds on what the other person says, rather than blocking or redirecting. You'll do this in pairs, then small groups, then as a full team.\n\nThe last hour involves longer-form exercises that map directly onto real work scenarios: handling unexpected feedback, staying present in a chaotic meeting, listening without preparing your reply. No performance experience needed — some of the best sessions involve people who said they'd be terrible at this."},{"id":"9","featured":true,"slug":"kids-pottery-holland-village","title":"Kids Pottery Class","provider":"Clay Play Studio","image":"/images/gettyimages-1345717721-660c27be6aad2.avif","description":"Hands-on clay sessions designed for kids aged 5–12. They build, squish, and shape — and walk away with something fired and glazed to take home. Parents welcome to join.","category":"Craft","location":"Holland Village","duration":"1.5h","price":48,"pax":"1–10 kids","tags":["kids-parents","educational","creative"],"images":[],"host":{"name":"Min Chen","bio":"Min has been a ceramics artist and educator for over a decade. She designed the Clay Play curriculum specifically for children aged 5–12, with a focus on sensory exploration over precision. She genuinely believes clay is one of the most honest materials a child can work with."},"whatToExpect":"Kids start with a ball of air-dry clay and zero instructions. Min observes what each child naturally gravitates toward before gently guiding them toward a finished piece — usually a small animal, a bowl, or whatever they've decided to make that day.\n\nParents are welcome to sit alongside and join in. The studio is set up so adults can work on their own piece while keeping an eye on their child.\n\nFinished pieces are left to dry and can be collected 3–5 days later, glazed and ready to take home. Min photographs every piece before collection so you have a record even if it doesn't survive the MRT ride."},{"id":"11","slug":"nature-journal-botanic-gardens","title":"Hydroponics for Growing Healthy Salad Greens","provider":"The Living Centre","category":"Outdoor","location":"Botanic Gardens","duration":"2h","price":38,"pax":"1–15","featured":false,"tags":["kids-parents","introvert","educational"],"description":"$4","image":"/images/1779196429151-tkwbd3t5eem.png","images":[],"host":{"name":"The Living Centre","bio":"What you will learn Choose the Best Salad greens for Singapore’s climate that are delicious and healthy  (e.g. right varieties of lettuce, kale…and many others) Using Sunlight to keep your cost low in hydroponics"},"whatToExpect":" No soil, no mess – just clean, fast, space-saving growing Understand Safety in Hydroponics – we teach you how to identify safe materials to use in hydropoics Plant, Grow, and Harvest with confidence—learn when to sow, how to water, and when to harvest for maximum flavor and nutrition. Grow in Small Spaces using our techniques, ideal for balconies, HDB flats, condominium .  Techniques also applies to landed property What's Included 25 Comprehensive Video Lessons covering every stage of your hydroponics salad greens journey. Total Duration is 2 Hours.  Access anytime , anywhere for the entire 1 year Downloadable Slides, Guides & Checklists so you can follow along easily even at the end of the course. Early Bird BONUS #1  GrowThrive Hydroponics Kit (include all you need to start hydroponics at home) Worth SG$45 (only during promo period) Early Bird BONUS #2 FREE One year one-to-one support from Expert Training Team (You can ask them questions and they support you to grow salad greens using hydroponics!) "},{"id":"2","slug":"sip-and-paint-tanjong-pagar","title":"Professional Oil Painting Trial Art Class | Art Course | Art Lesson (Suitable for beginners I All art materials provided)","provider":"Canvas & Co.","category":"Art","location":"Tanjong Pagar","duration":"2.5h","price":75,"pax":"1–20","featured":true,"tags":["burned-out","introvert","creative"],"description":"Wine, brushes, and zero judgment. A casual guided painting session where the vibe matters more than the art. Great for solo evenings or small groups.","image":"/images/1779196236682-ou21s0w9nwa.jpg","images":["/images/1779196243159-qxt1mw57dn.jpg"],"host":{"name":"Visual Arts Centre Singapore","bio":"Canvas & Co. was founded by two art school graduates who wanted to make painting social rather than precious. They've hosted over 1,000 sessions and have a strict no-judgment policy that they take very seriously."},"whatToExpect":"You'll arrive to find your canvas set up with a light pencil sketch guide and your first glass of wine poured. The session is guided — a Canvas & Co. artist walks through the painting step by step — but the pace is loose and the music is good.\n\nThe subject changes each session: landscapes, botanicals, abstract colour fields. You won't know the exact painting until you arrive, which keeps regulars coming back.\n\nEveryone leaves with a finished (or at least complete) piece. Canvas & Co. provides all materials — brushes, acrylics, canvas, aprons. Just bring yourself and a willingness to ruin a shirt."},{"id":"1","slug":"terrarium-making-queenstown","title":"Terrarium Making","provider":"The Green Fingers Studio","category":"Craft","location":"Queenstown","duration":"2h","price":68,"pax":"1–8","featured":true,"tags":["burned-out","introvert","solo"],"description":"Build your own little world in a glass jar. No prior experience needed — just a love for plants and a willingness to get your hands dirty. Perfect for unwinding after a long week.","image":"/images/1779196486313-75g9lk8v8p3.jpg","images":[],"host":{"name":"The Green Fingers Team","bio":"The Green Fingers Studio team are plant obsessives who left corporate jobs to spend their days surrounded by moss and succulents. They've taught over 3,000 people to build terrariums and still get excited when someone makes their first one."},"whatToExpect":"You'll choose your vessel from a selection of glass containers — open bowls, closed ecosystems, geometric shapes — and then your plants from the studio's resident collection of ferns, moss, succulents, and air plants.\n\nThe team guides you through layering: drainage gravel, activated charcoal, soil mix, then planting. The process takes about 90 minutes if you're decisive, longer if you're the type who rearranges things eight times.\n\nYou'll leave with a fully assembled terrarium and a care card specific to your plant selection. Terrariums that are well-matched to their environment can last for years with minimal attention."}]}],["$L5"],"$L6"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"GtlyCSOmbjc6KDs2gevVf"}
